<title>USA: St Joseph hogs off $1.00 - USDA.</title>
<headline>St Joseph hogs off $1.00 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>ST JOSEPH 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA said compared with</p>
<p>Wednesday, barrows and gilts were $1.00 lower.  Top $53.50 per</p>
<p>cwt.</p>
<p>Snow storm moving into this area but expected to go South of hog country. At current cut-outs packers not interested in building big inventory for Saturday kill.</p>
<p>    US 1-3    230-270 lbs    53.00-53.50</p>
<p>    US 2-3    270-290 lbs    51.50-52.50</p>
<p>	   uniform US 1  214 lbs    52.50</p>
<p>Sows - steady/off $1.00. Top $54.00.</p>
<p>    US 1-2    300-450 lbs    44.50</p>
<p>		  450-500 lbs    47.00</p>
<p>    US 1-3    500-550 lbs    50.00</p>
<p>		  550-700 lbs    53.00-54.00</p>
<p>    Boars - 300-700 lbs    41.00</p>
<p>		200-300 lbs    42.00</p>
</text>
